  "conventions": {
    "preparation": "Intake 0.0373999726942. Four real, disjoint sin² windows of width H/4 on one arm with the existing cosine dipole angular factor and mirrored scalar-well displacement. One draining carrier arm. Phasors exp(-i omega t). All other wall coordinates and sidebands clamped. Results per unit peak displacement in source window; response work conjugate to the identical test window in read quarter.",
    "fluid": "Stationary Neumann trace, spatial and temporal dipole tractions generalized to each window. Half energy Hessian. F_ext=-S† A^-1 S/2. Positive emitted work checked at two enclosing cuts for pure drives and a complex superposition. Same 6R real-plus-outgoing domain as archived spectral calculation. This is the induced fluid response; any additional static contact/pinning must be separately specified.",
    "wave": "Fixed-action single scalar support. Direct hessian and both ws±omega contractions. The lower satellite is below continuum, the upper is outgoing. Absorption identity on full matrix. Response applies to pump-cycle-averaged clamped same-tone loads. Compared carrier cells 32 and 64, scalar spacings .04 and .025, with absorber box and strength also changed. Finite-grid samples are not continuum extrapolations.",
    "material": "Conditional rest-frame simple front with speed squared equal to constant tension / wall mass per area. Fully normal inertia and both-arm radial calibration; identical halves. Neglect advection, dispersion, noise and extra losses in intrinsic transit controls. h(u)=(1+8 sin^8(pi(u-s)))/mean, with s=0 and 0.15. Front transit H/c_uniform times integral sqrt(h). M_b=M_radial/3 integral h sin^4(pi u). Normalized total mass and slowness integral are invariant under the shift. Report selective two-preparation readout with same field kernels and stiffness as the archived bend; raw dipole line is distinct.",
    "interval_bound": "Let v=c_uniform/c(u) with integral v²=1, g=sin⁴(pi u). Station times give cell means vbar. V=1−integral vbar². B=sum vbar_i² integral_i(g−gbar_i)². Since residual v−vbar integrates to zero in each cell, the mixed term in integral g v² has magnitude ≤2 sqrt(V B); the square-residual term lies between 0 and V. Intersect with [0,1], scale by M_radial/3. This outer enclosure needs exact intrinsic times and radial calibration. Four projected force windows and two tones do not supply the 16 station data."
  },
  "review": {
    "verdict": "Scoped clear for the two-tone clamped field loads, the conditional travel-time bounds, and the one- versus two-peak control.",
    "scope": "Independent source audit and guarded Fourier projection, transit quadrature and separate lineshape inversion with linear interpolation. Verified force signs, angular and source factors, direct term, pump sidebands, finite-area enclosure and the recorded controls.",
    "limitations": "Measured phase and clamped force are not an intrinsic wall transit. Coarse/fine variation in the fluid load; reference plane, Doppler shift, mode mixing and frequency coverage matter. Contributions with free wall harmonics must be combined before elimination. Fold classification is restricted to the previously tested mass branch and selective readout. No new moving-mouth 0PN inertia."
  },
